# 2.1 What is a Series?

A **Series** is the simplest data structure in Pandas.

It is a **one-dimensional labeled array** capable of storing almost any type of data.

Think of it as **one column of an Excel sheet**.

Example:

| Index | Name  |
| ----: | ----- |
|     0 | Rahul |
|     1 | Amit  |
|     2 | Priya |
|     3 | Neha  |

This entire column is a **Series**.

---

## Definition

> A Series consists of **two parts**:

* Values
* Index (Labels)

Example

```python
import pandas as pd

students = pd.Series(["Rahul","Amit","Priya","Neha"])

print(students)
```

Output

```
0    Rahul
1     Amit
2    Priya
3     Neha
dtype: object
```

Notice something.

```
0
1
2
3
```

These are called the **Index**.

```
Rahul
Amit
Priya
Neha
```

These are the **Values**.

---

# Internal Structure

Every Series has three important components.

```
Series

│

├── Index

├── Values

└── Data Type (dtype)
```

Example

```
