Blue

Red

NaN

Green
```

Most frequent value

```
Red
```

```python
s.fillna(s.mode()[0])
```

Output

```
Red

Blue

Red

Red

Green
```

---

# Common Mistakes

### ❌ Filling every column with `0`

Not appropriate for all data.

Example:

```
Age

NaN
```

Age is not necessarily 0.

---

### ❌ Dropping all missing rows

You may lose a significant portion of your dataset.

---

### ❌ Ignoring missing values

Many ML algorithms will fail or produce unreliable results.

